@startuml
title EventFlow — C4 Level 2: Implemented Prototype Containers
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Customer / API Client" as User

node "Docker Host" {
  rectangle "eventflow-api\n[Docker Container]\n.NET 8 ASP.NET Core" as API #B8D5F2 {
    rectangle "WebAPI\nREST Controller" as Web
    rectangle "Application\nCreateBookingUseCase" as App
    rectangle "Domain\nBooking model" as Domain
    rectangle "Infrastructure\nInMemory adapters" as Infra
    rectangle "Messaging\nInMemory EventBus" as Bus
    rectangle "Notification Consumer" as Notify
    rectangle "Analytics Consumer" as Analytics
    rectangle "Events\nIntegration event contracts" as Events
  }
}

User --> Web : HTTP / JSON\nTCP 8080
Web --> App : In-process call
App --> Domain : Domain rules
App --> Infra : Repository / availability ports
App --> Bus : Publish BookingCreatedEvent
Bus --> Notify : Async dispatch
Bus --> Analytics : Async dispatch

rectangle "PostgreSQL / Redis / OIDC /\nPayment / Email" as Target #FCE5CD
Target .. API : Planned integrations\nNot deployed in prototype

note bottom of API
  Current deployment: one application container.
  InMemory data is lost after process restart.
  No external broker or database is connected.
end note
@enduml
